A||||13||S. Goertzen||Fiero Pace Car||||1||
Z||000000||S. Goertzen||05-13-2001||06:25 PM||||I'm looking for all the information possible on the Fiero Pace Car. I've been told that they were only released with the super duty 2.5L four lunger, but the one around here has a 2.8L V-6 in it. Is my info wrong or is this a fake. Are there any other tell tale signs that one can look for? Are there any good web sites that I can check out that May help? This car looks great, but the owner insists that it's authentic and I'd like to find out for sure. Thanks guys.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||05-13-2001||06:35 PM||||Indy only caame with a 4. They also only came in 84 when all fieros had 4's. So either its a later year with indy stuff or its an indy with a 6. I have heard putting a 6 in an 84 is not fun. The best way is to check the tag on the fender well under the hood. It is a sticker on the driver side wheel well.If its real it will have a Y82 code on that tag. Also the 10th leter in the vin denotes the year with E being 84 F being 85 G being 86 H being 87 and J being 88||||reg||1
Z||000002||S. Goertzen||05-13-2001||07:34 PM||||Thanks, that's a huge help. I definately think that it's a wannabe now, because I'm sure that he said it's an '86.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-13-2001||07:49 PM||||Let see if I can remember what they had. They all have pale grey interior with leather wheel and shift knob and leather armrests. Leater seats with a red cloth insert with the indy logo. Red carpet and red lower door carpet. White stock aluminum rims with a red pinstripe. Stripped air filter top and rocker box.<BR>Of course the Indy nose and fender badges. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||05-13-2001||09:16 PM||||HI, I agree with all the above, i currently own 2 indy's, like said above, all came with 4 cyl engine, y82 code, light grey steering wheel and door handles, if you have any other questions on indys, feel free to email me...Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
Z||000005||S. Goertzen||05-13-2001||10:13 PM||||Thanks, that confirms it, it's not authentic. Now I'll just have to find a build sheet or something that I can print out that will prove to him that he is wrong. He is very adament that it is truly a pace car and worth a lot of $$$, and that the person that he got it from simply didn't know what they had before, which is why it was the wrong color etc... Thanks again guys.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mbramble||05-13-2001||10:36 PM||||Just get the VIN number (from thru the front windshield, behind the driver's side dash) and check it at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/vin.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/vin.html</A> <P>If it shows up as anything other than 84, it is definitely not an Indy.||||reg||1
Z||000007||84Bill||05-13-2001||10:42 PM||||WOOOHOOO I got one today! 400 bucks and drove her home take a look but I'll warn you she aint pretty<BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||FieroLisa||05-13-2001||10:46 PM||||The Fiero that actually paced the race had a 232 hp 2.7L with a 3 speed automatic. Buuuut you're not going to find those running around anywhere, I think they are in museums or something. 2000 commemorative cars were produce, but they were the 2.5L.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/daytona1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||05-13-2001||10:47 PM||||BTW it will come up as an 84 SE but the number will most likely be like mine. Got to the bottom of my page below and see what it looks like.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy/image0110.jpg">  <P> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||S. Goertzen||05-13-2001||11:34 PM||||84Bill - OUCH! I'm scrolling down thinking that's not to bad, then the pic of the passenger side rear appears. A little work needed, but still a great buy. FieroLisa - too bad they're in museums. Dad owns a performance shop and his partner has a 2M4 that he traded for two cv axles for a buick something or other that he paid 25 bucks for. We've got another 2.5 from a Cavalier or something with a swirl port head. We ported and polished the head, polished and balanced the rotating assembly, etc, etc. We're working on a quad carb conversion for it to. He figures that we should get about 235 hp before the bottle (likely a 100 shot). It should be kinda wild. I'd like to set it up for street courses or something.||||reg||1
